*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
*      MDATA -- machine-dependent data for the Go SIL machine
*
*      S4D58 6.20 requires four character strings and 4.2 requires the
*      syntax tables.  Neither can be written as SIL text: a character
*      literal cannot contain a quotation mark (7.6: "Quotation marks
*      do not occur within literals"), the collating sequence contains
*      control characters, and a syntax table is 256 entries of data
*      that Appendix A specifies in a different language altogether.
*
*      This segment therefore reserves the space and leaves the content
*      to the loader.  That is a deviation from the letter of two
*      programming notes -- 6.17 note 1 says every character a BUFFER
*      assembles must be blank at the start of execution, and 6.12 note
*      1 says every field an ARRAY assembles must be zero -- and it is
*      deliberate: BUFFER and ARRAY are being used here as the only
*      documented ways to reserve characters and descriptors, not for
*      their initial values.  Nothing in the SNOBOL4 source reads any
*      of these regions before the loader has filled them.
*
*      The syntax tables are filled by pkg/sil/asm, from the
*      descriptions of Appendix A held in pkg/sil/syntab.  4.2 asks for
*      exactly that: the tables "are generated from such descriptions
*      using a (SNOBOL4) program in which the character classes and the
*      order of the internal character codes are parameters.  The use
*      of some kind of automatic technique to generate the syntax
*      tables is advisable, both to ensure accuracy and because of the
*      large amount of data involved."
*
*      6.20 note 1 permits this: "COPY may be implemented in a variety
*      of ways.  COPY may, for example, simply expand into the data
*      required, depending on the value of its argument."
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
*
*      Character Strings (S4D58 6.20)
*
*      The SNOBOL4 source assembles the specifiers ALPHSP, AMPSP, COLSP
*      and QTSP against these four addresses (lines 5612-5620), so what
*      is needed here is the address of the characters, not a specifier
*      in front of them.  Each region is exactly as long as the
*      specifier that points at it says it is.
*
ALPHA  BUFFER  ALPHSZ		   Collating sequence, ALPHSP
AMPST  BUFFER  1		   Ampersand, AMPSP
COLSTR BUFFER  2		   Colon and a blank, COLSP
QTSTR  BUFFER  1		   Quotation mark, QTSP
*
*      Syntax Tables (S4D58 4.2, Appendix A)
*
*      A syntax table has one entry per character of the character set,
*      indexed by the character's internal code, and an entry has three
*      fields: the next table address A, the indicator T, and the put
*      field P (5.1).  That is the shape of a descriptor, so E -- the
*      address width of a syntax table entry (5.3) -- is DESCR here,
*      and a table is ALPHSZ descriptors.
*
*      Appendix A defines all twenty-five.  Thirteen are named by the
*      SNOBOL4 source; the other twelve are reached only through a
*      GOTO(TABLE) action inside another table, and are marked below.
*
*      4.2: only SNABTB is modified during execution, by CLERTB and
*      PLUGTB.  The other twenty-four are constant.
*
BIOPTB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Binary operator
CARDTB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Card image
DQLITB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Double-quoted literal    (reached by GOTO)
ELEMTB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Element
EOSTB  ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   End of statement
FLITB  ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Real literal 	    (reached by GOTO)
FRWDTB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Forward scan
GOTFTB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Failure goto 	    (reached by GOTO)
GOTOTB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Goto field
GOTSTB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Success goto 	    (reached by GOTO)
IBLKTB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Initial blanks
INTGTB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Integer		    (reached by GOTO)
LBLTB  ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Label
LBLXTB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Label, extended
NBLKTB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Nonblank		    (reached by GOTO)
NUMBTB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Number
NUMCTB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Number continuation	    (reached by GOTO)
SNABTB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   SPAN, NOTANY, ANY, BREAK
SQLITB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Single-quoted literal    (reached by GOTO)
STARTB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Statement start	    (reached by GOTO)
TBLKTB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Trailing blanks	    (reached by GOTO)
UNOPTB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Unary operator
VARATB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Variable, first character
VARBTB ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Variable, later characters (reached by GOTO)
VARTB  ARRAY   ALPHSZ		   Variable		    (reached by GOTO)
